{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing distance measurement is the trace, and it defeats the claim. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the field that governs the threshold test, and trip_record.actual_distance_km a rounded convenience copy that may not be cited for it. The trace is 3.96 km and the booked optimal on EV-TRIP-02843 is 3.2 km, so the measured excess is 0.76 km - exactly what the trace's own derived block reports at derived.deviation.excess_km. That figure is below the 0.8 km absolute gate POL-RD-01 sets, and it is not greater than it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02843", "EV-TRIP-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both limbs of POL-RD-01 must pass, and here only one does. The percentage limb is satisfied - derived.deviation.excess_pct is 23.75 against a 20.0 threshold - but the absolute limb is not, and because the establishment test is conjunctive the code-computed reading of this same trace is derived.deviation.status = 'no deviation'. POL-RD-01 then says in terms that if either establishment test fails, no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider's own claim text - '3.96 km' - is the very figure that fails the gate.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The result does not turn on which distance figure is used, because the absolute gate fails on both. The trace's 3.96 km yields 0.76 km of excess; even the trip record's rounded actual_distance_km of 4.0 km yields 0.80 km, and 0.80 is not greater than 0.8 km - the test is 'greater than', not 'at least'. POL-RD-01 also directs that the rounded copy may not be cited for this test at all. There is no arithmetic on this record under which the rider reaches the threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02843", "EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged it. POL-RD-08(b) requires the rider to show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace; this trace is unimpaired on any view - 100.0% coverage, 45 fixes at the expected 10 second interval, no gaps and a 0.0 second max gap, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is not engaged - and it shows 0.76 km. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver, and the driver is not called on to invoke POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12 at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02843", "EV-TRIP-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-02 does not run, and with it every distance-and-time refund route for the rider closes. The clause applies only 'where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01', and none is. The fare block's figures are therefore conditional, not owed: recomputed_fare 8.68 and refund_before_rounding 0.96 are what would apply if a deviation existed, and no deviation does. On EV-FARE-02843 the trip is METERED with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The charge of 9.64 is simply the rate card applied to the trip actually driven: 3.80 base fare, 3.00 distance (4.0 km at 0.75), 2.04 time (7.3 min at 0.28) and the 0.80 platform fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02843", "EV-TRIP-02843", "EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-empting the smallest point available to the rider: the billed distance (distance_charged_km 4.0) exceeds the trace (3.96 km) by 0.04 km, about SGD 0.03 at the 0.75 per km rate. That is the rounding POL-RD-01 identifies between the trace and its convenience copy on the trip record, and it is not a billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4), whose subject-matter is unmatched gantry lines and misapplied surcharges - this fare breakdown carries zero ERP lines, zero tolls and zero surcharges, so that limb has nothing to correct.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02843", "EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern can be built against this driver. POL-RD-06 is engaged only by a MATERIAL deviation, and materiality requires an excess above 50.0% of optimal or above 8.0 km; the measured excess is 0.76 km and 23.75%, so the provision is not reached. Even if the profile were consulted, the only citable fields on EV-DPROF-02843 are deviation_flags_90d = 1 against completed_trips_90d = 228 - a ratio of 0.44%, below both the 3-flag test and the 5% test with at least 40 trips. Every other field on that profile (rating, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags, acceptance_rate and the rest) is context only and may not ground any finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02843", "EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's on-record note about one-way streets is not advanced as a defence and needs no supporting record. POL-RD-13 tests an external-cause assertion only against a traffic advisory for the trip, and the driver names no advisory and cites no evidence ID for one, so under POL-RD-13(1) the assertion cannot operate as an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact. The driver's case does not require it: the POL-RD-01 gate fails on this trip's own trace, which is where the finding must rest.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome the evidence supports is NO_ACTION on this rider-filed dispute, and on a rider-filed dispute that is a driver win. POL-GEN-03 defines NO_ACTION party-relatively: the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands, with fare_breakdown.payment_status and fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd left as they are - here CHARGED and 0.00. The rider's contested 2.00 is not returned, the metered charge of 9.64 stays with the driver, and no escalation trigger fires because the deciding fact is carried by artifacts at full weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02843", "EV-GPS-02843"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is decided on the platform's own measurements, and the outcome is NO_ACTION — the metered charge of SGD 9.64 stands and nothing is refunded. On a rider-filed dispute that leaves the charge in place.\n\nTHE DISTANCE. POL-RD-01 makes the GPS trace the governing measurement. The trace (EV-GPS-02843) recorded 3.96 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff events, against a booked optimal of 3.2 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02843). The excess is 0.76 km, which is 23.75% of the optimal. The clause requires BOTH limbs to pass: the excess must be greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. The 23.75% figure passes; the 0.76 km figure does not, and the rider's claim falls 0.04 km short of the gate. The answer does not change if the trip record's rounded 4.0 km is used instead — that yields exactly 0.80 km, and the test is 'greater than 0.8', not 'at least 0.8' — and POL-RD-01 in any event forbids citing that rounded convenience copy for the threshold test. The platform's own derivation reads derived.deviation.status = 'no deviation'. No deviation is therefore established, and POL-RD-02 never runs: the figures the rider placed on the record (recomputed_fare SGD 8.68, refund before rounding SGD 0.96, payable SGD 1.00) are conditional arithmetic, not an amount owed. The rider's request for SGD 1.00 is not granted; the SGD 2.00 contested is not returned and the SGD 9.64 charge stands.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The driver's note 'one-way streets' asserts an external traffic cause, and there is no traffic advisory for this trip to test it against: EV-ADVIS-02843-01 is MISSING and carries weight_multiplier 0.0. Under POL-RD-13 such an assertion, made with no advisory on file and no advisory identifier cited, carries no weight under POL-RD-08; and because the driver named no advisory ID, the absence is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not triggered. That makes no difference to the result: the outcome rests on the POL-RD-01 gate on this trip's own trace, which the driver does not need the note to win.\n\nBILLING INTEGRITY. POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to correct. EV-FARE-02843 carries no ERP lines, no tolls and no surcharges, so there is no unmatched gantry and no misapplied airport surcharge. The billed distance of 4.0 km exceeds the trace's 3.96 km by 0.04 km — about SGD 0.03 at the 0.75 per km rate — which is the rounding POL-RD-01 identifies between the trace and its convenience copy, not a billing defect. The SGD 9.64 charged is fully accounted for: base fare SGD 3.80 + distance SGD 3.00 + time SGD 2.04 + platform fee SGD 0.80.\n\nBURDEN AND PROFILES. The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged it: the excess shown on an unimpaired trace — 45 fixes, a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is not engaged — falls below the POL-RD-01 gate. The burden never shifts, so the driver is not called on to invoke POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12; and in any event the chat log is empty, there is no pickup or dropoff amendment and no amended optimal, the fare model is METERED and the vehicle type is RYDE_X rather than pooled. The rider's POL-RD-08 profile gate is not met (deviation_claims_60d = 1, so no extra corroboration is demanded beyond the trace), but that does not repair the shortfall. POL-RD-06 is not engaged because this is not a material deviation; the driver's only citable counters are deviation_flags_90d = 1 against completed_trips_90d = 228, below both the 3-flag test and the 5%-with-40-trips test. Every other field on either profile is context only and has grounded no finding.\n\nESCALATION AND CONFIDENCE. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired, the trip identifiers and timestamps agree across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, no charge line lacks a counterpart, and confidence is above the platform floor. Confidence is 0.95, and the cap is 1.0 — the minimum weight of the artifacts that carry the deciding fact (the trace and the trip record, each weight_multiplier 1.0). The missing advisory carries no fact and does not move that cap. The monetary effect of this ruling is nil, so there is nothing to execute or hold."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
